course: dictionary
lesson: 15676
title: One word, more than one meaning
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: Some words have more than one meaning, and the context tells you which one the writer means. «Are you ticklish?» asks Mia, and she means easily made to laugh when someone touches you. Ticklish is an adjective, so it describes a person, a foot or a rib.
explain: Read on: «The question was ticklish, so the teacher took her time to answer it.» Ticklish does not mean funny here. The clues are the question and took her time, so it means difficult and needing careful handling.
explain: A third meaning is a light itchy feeling. «My throat felt ticklish, so I coughed.» Ask yourself: what word would fit here? Then put your meaning into the sentence and check that it still makes sense.
fact: Ticklish means easily made to laugh or squirm when someone tickles you.
fact: «Ticklish» can also mean difficult and needing careful handling, as in «a ticklish question».
fact: «Ticklish» can mean a light itchy feeling, as in «a ticklish cough».
fact: Many people are most ticklish on the feet, the sides and the ribs.
fact: Scientists think you cannot tickle yourself because your brain predicts your own touch. Tickling must stop when someone says stop.
exercise: «Dad's feet are very ticklish, so he squirms when we touch them.» What does ticklish mean here? | Difficult to solve | *Easily made to laugh or squirm | Very cold and wet | Hard to see
exercise: Ben says, «The maths question was ticklish.» What does ticklish mean here? | Easily made to laugh | *Difficult and needing careful handling | Very quick | Light and itchy
exercise: Which sentence uses ticklish to mean a light itchy feeling? | «Her ticklish answer was correct.» | «The ticklish fox ran away.» | «Our ticklish teacher gave us a test.» | *«My nose felt ticklish before I sneezed.»
test: «The ticklish job needed a steady hand.» What does ticklish mean in this sentence? | Very wet and slippery | *Difficult and needing careful handling | A light itchy feeling | Easily made to laugh
test: Lily says, «Dad is ticklish under his arms.» Why does she say this? | He is difficult to talk to | He is cold and wet | He has an itchy rash | *He is easily made to laugh or squirm when tickled
exam: «The ticklish question made the whole class go quiet.» What does ticklish mean in this sentence? | *Difficult and needing careful handling | A light itchy feeling | Easily made to laugh or squirm | Very funny and loud
